From 31d2608c7064a72f69c28c6e53565c1b5a4dbaa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 18:42:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation/dax: dax/kmem private-node ABIs

dax/kmem grows the following attributes:
 - private     : set hotplug NUMA node to N_MEMORY_PRIVATE
 - dax_file    : allow mmap() against the character device
 - reclaim     : enable NODE_PRIVATE_CAP_RECLAIM
 - user_numa   : enable NODE_PRIVATE_CAP_USER_NUMA
 - hotunplug   : enable NODE_PRIVATE_CAP_HOTUNPLUG
 - kernel_numa : enable NODE_PRIVATE_CAP_KERNEL_NUMA
 - ltpin       : enable NODE_PRIVATE_CAP_LTPIN

Signed-off-by: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
---
 Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax | 78 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 77 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax
index 60703fffa99..6f2d5fc17e4 100644
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax
@@ -157,7 +157,11 @@ Contact:	nvdimm@lists.linux.dev
 Description:
 		(RW) Controls the state of the memory region.
 		Applies to all memory blocks associated with the device.
-		Only applies to dax_kmem devices.
+		Applies to the dax_kmem driver.  When the device's "private"
+		attribute is set the memory is onlined onto a private
+		(N_MEMORY_PRIVATE) node and the per-service opt-ins below select
+		which mm services may touch it; otherwise it is onlined as
+		ordinary system RAM.
 
 		Reading returns the current state; the writable states mirror
 		the per-block /sys/devices/system/memory/memoryX/state ABI::
@@ -175,3 +179,75 @@ Description:
 		A device can only be onlined from the "unplugged" state, so a
 		device must be returned to "unplugged" before it can be onlined
 		into a different state.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/private
+Date:		June, 2026
+KernelVersion:	v6.21
+Contact:	nvdimm@lists.linux.dev
+Description:
+		(RW) dax_kmem only.  When set, the device onlines its memory as a
+		private (N_MEMORY_PRIVATE) node instead of ordinary system RAM,
+		and the per-service opt-ins below become visible.  When clear (the
+		default) the device behaves as classic kmem system RAM.  Writable
+		only while the device is "unplugged" (-EBUSY otherwise).
+
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/dax_file
+Date:		June, 2026
+KernelVersion:	v6.21
+Contact:	nvdimm@lists.linux.dev
+Description:
+		(RW) dax_kmem only.  When set, mmap()ing the /dev/daxX.Y char
+		device yields an ordinary ANONYMOUS mapping whose faults (and
+		swap-in) are bound to the device's node, i.e. a way to fault
+		anonymous memory onto a specific node through the dax device.
+		This is independent of "private": it is a dax-only extension, not
+		an mm-service capability, so it is its own toggle rather than a
+		per-node opt-in.  When clear (the default) no cdev is installed
+		and opening /dev/daxX.Y returns -ENXIO (classic kmem behaviour).
+		Writable only while the device is "unplugged" (-EBUSY otherwise).
+
+		Faults are base-page (PAGE_SIZE) only unless the node opts into
+		reclaim (the "reclaim" attr), because a node that cannot
+		compact/reclaim risks failing higher-order (THP) allocations for
+		want of a given order; with reclaim, THP is allowed.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/reclaim
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/user_numa
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/hotunplug
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/demotion
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/numa_balancing
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/ltpin
+Date:		June, 2026
+KernelVersion:	v6.21
+Contact:	nvdimm@lists.linux.dev
+Description:
+		(RW) dax_kmem "private" mode only (hidden otherwise).
+
+		Per-service opt-ins (booleans) recorded on the device and
+		applied to its private node at hotplug, selecting which mm
+		services may act on the node's memory.
+
+		All services opted-out by default.
+
+		  reclaim		allow reclaim of the node's folios, by
+		                        the mm and by userspace madvise.
+
+		  user_numa		allow userspace placement and migration
+		                        via mempolicy and move/migrate_pages.
+
+		  hotunplug		allow hot-unplug via migration
+
+		  demotion		allow reclaim to demote/tier onto the
+		                        node (requires reclaim)
+
+		  numa_balancing	allow NUMA balancing to scan and
+		                        migrate the node's folios
+
+		  ltpin			allow FOLL_LONGTERM GUP pins
+
+		Writable only while the device is "unplugged" (-EBUSY otherwise).
+
+		Dependencies between opt-ins (demotion requires reclaim) are
+		validated when the device is hotplugged, not at write time.
+		An inconsistent combination is accepted by the write but the
+		subsequent hotplug fails.
-- 
